WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:01.740
- [Instructor] Let's
see if we can figure out

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:06.000
what 2 1/4 times three is.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.563
Pause this video and see
if you can work that out.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.270
All right, now there's different ways

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.520
that we could approach this.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.620
One way to approach this is to recognize

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.410
that if I multiply anything times three,

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.220
that means that I'm taking
three of these things

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.240
and adding them together.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.210
So, this is going to be the same thing

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:28.210
as 2 1/4 plus 2 1/4 plus 2 1/4.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.420
Now, I could also view
this as each of these 2 1/4

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.420
is two plus 1/4 plus two
plus 1/4 plus two plus 1/4.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.550
All I did is I broke up each of the 2 1/4

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.250
into a two plus 1/4.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.870
And then what I could do is

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.310
I could add the whole number parts,

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:54.310
two plus two plus two is
going to be equal to six.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:59.590
And then, if I were to
take 1/4 plus 1/4 plus 1/4,

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:01.430
how many fourths do I now have?

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:06.020
I have 3/4, so it's gonna be six plus 3/4,

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.983
or I could write this as 6 3/4.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:16.030
Now, another way that we
could have approached this

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:19.350
is we could've rewritten 2 1/4.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:24.350
I could have rewritten that as
the same thing as two is 8/4,

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.140
8/4 is the same thing as two,

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:31.720
plus 1/4 and then I'm multiplying

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.290
that whole thing times three.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:35.970
And so, this is going to be the same thing

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:40.970
as 9/4, 8/4 plus 1/4 is 9/4, times three.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.667
And so, we could say, "Hey,
that's just going to be equal

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:49.667
"to 9/4 plus 9/4 plus 9/4,
which would be equal to what?"

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.210
Well, I have,

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.960
this is going to be nine
plus nine plus nine fourths,

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.220
which is going to be equal to 27/4.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.107
Now, you might be saying,

00:02:02.107 --> 00:02:05.130
"Hey, these look like they are different",

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:06.160
but you could check this.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.760
Six is equal to how many fourths?

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.520
So, six is equal to 24/4,

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:17.520
24/4 plus 3/4, which is
exactly equal to 27/4.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.263
And we are done.

